# Phase 3 — Sub-10ms Redirection with Redis Cache-Aside

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Implement the Cache-Aside pattern in Redis to resolve shortcodes into destination URLs with sub-10ms response times. Understand the trade-offs between HTTP 301 and 302 redirects, and protect your cache against Stampede events.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### HTTP 301 (Permanent) vs 302 (Found / Temporary)

| Status Code | Browser Caching | Analytics Impact | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|
| **301 Moved Permanently** | Browser caches redirect forever | **Destroys analytics** (browser never visits your server again) | Permanent domain migrations |
| **302 Found (Temporary)** | Browser requests your server on every click | **Accurate clickstream** on 100% of visits | **URL Shorteners & Tracking** |

For an analytics-driven shortener, **HTTP 302 is mandatory**.

### The Cache-Aside Flow

```
Request: GET /r/{shortCode}
   │
   ├──► 1. Query Redis: GET url:{shortCode}
   │         │
   │         ├──► Hit: Return 302 to destination (< 3ms)
   │         │
   │         └──► Miss: Query PostgreSQL
   │                     │
   │                     ├──► Found: SET url:{shortCode} in Redis (TTL 24h)
   │                     │    Return 302
   │                     └──► Not Found: Return 404
```

---

## 🛠 Step-by-Step Implementation

### Step 1 · Build the Redirect Controller

Create `backend/src/controllers/redirect.controller.ts`:

```typescript
import { Request, Response } from 'express';
import { redisClient } from '../config/redis';
import { prisma } from '../config/prisma';

const CACHE_TTL_SECONDS = 86400; // 24 hours

export class RedirectController {
  public static async handleRedirect(req: Request, res: Response): Promise<void> {
    const { shortCode } = req.params;
    const cacheKey = `url:${shortCode}`;

    try {
      // 1. Try Redis cache
      const cachedDestination = await redisClient.get(cacheKey);
      if (cachedDestination) {
        // Queue click tracking event (implemented in Phase 5)
        // Stream: 'stream:clicks'
        res.redirect(302, cachedDestination);
        return;
      }

      // 2. Cache miss: fallback to DB
      const record = await prisma.url.findUnique({
        where: { shortCode },
        select: { id: true, originalUrl: true }
      });

      if (!record) {
        res.status(404).json({ error: 'Short URL not found' });
        return;
      }

      // 3. Populate Redis Cache
      await redisClient.setEx(cacheKey, CACHE_TTL_SECONDS, record.originalUrl);

      res.redirect(302, record.originalUrl);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Redirect error:', err);
      res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
    }
  }
}
```

