# Phase 8 — Manual Interventions & Dead-Letter Replay

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Build manual operational intervention tools: inspect failed job stack traces in modal dialogs, edit payload parameters to fix schema errors, and trigger single-click re-queueing from the Dead Letter Queue back into active processing.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

### The Human-in-the-Loop Fix Workflow

In real operations, tasks often fail because of bad input data (e.g. an invalid email address format or a corrupted URL). Simply retrying the identical bad input fails every time.

We provide an operational replay API:
1. Open failed job.
2. Inspect stack trace.
3. Modify the input JSON directly in the dashboard.
4. Re-inject into the queue: the job starts immediately with the corrected parameters.

---

## 🛠 Step-by-Step Implementation

### Step 1 · Replay API Endpoint

Create `backend/src/routes/replay.routes.ts`:

```typescript
import { Router, Request, Response } from 'express';
import { prisma } from '../config/prisma';
import { workflowQueue } from '../queues/orchestrator.queue';

const router = Router();

router.post('/:workflowId/retry', async (req: Request, res: Response) => {
  const { workflowId } = req.params;
  const { updatedPayload } = req.body;

  const workflow = await prisma.workflow.findUnique({ where: { id: workflowId } });
  if (!workflow) {
    res.status(404).json({ error: 'Workflow not found' });
    return;
  }

  // Update payload if corrected
  await prisma.workflow.update({
    where: { id: workflowId },
    data: {
      status: 'PENDING',
      error: null,
      payload: updatedPayload || workflow.payload
    }
  });

  // Re-enqueue in BullMQ
  await workflowQueue.add(workflow.name, { workflowId }, { priority: 1 });

  res.json({ message: 'Workflow re-queued successfully', workflowId });
});

export default router;
```

---

## ✅ Phase Checkpoint

- [ ] Triggering `POST /api/workflows/:id/retry` transitions a `FAILED` job back to `PENDING`
- [ ] The worker immediately re-claims the job and executes it
- [ ] Modified payload parameters are respected by the re-run

---

> **🧠 Key takeaway:** A Dead Letter Queue without a re-injection workflow is just a graveyard; adding parameter editing and replay turns it into a self-healing operational tool.

